  "acceptance_tolerance": 1e-10,
  "norms": "Frobenius matrix norms, maximum entrywise operator error as a second diagnostic, absolute scalar regression error.",
  "graph_checks": "Trace actual tensor-index operands and compare every ordered edge and boundary/MSB output; construct a separate named-edge reference encoding.",
  "ascent": "Reverse graph one tensor at a time on structural support. Cancel untouched tensor pairs by w\u2020w/u\u2020u. Touched tensors use local Heisenberg contraction with identity completion; exact declared identity gates become wire relabelings for the tree. Never construct or receive V in this path.",
  "support_rule": "Retain structural support even for zero or small coefficients. No numerical term pruning. Record support, retained/canceled tensors, identity removals, and temporary local dimensions at every step and stage.",
  "reference_comparator": "Construct full 256x256 O in MSB site order and compare complete logical 2x2 matrices V\u2020OV using the independent graph V and both saved implementations.",
  "regression": "Repeat 56 three-site flagged scores from the independent graph V with original entropy conventions; compare both original gaps.",
  "entropy": "Base 2; record raw eigenvalues; reject below -1e-10, exclude tolerated negatives only, retain all positive eigenvalues without trace renormalization.",
  "failure_rule": "Any topology mismatch or invariant failure is an audit failure. Preserve outputs and stop; do not alter architecture, leg ordering, or frozen inputs.",
